-- title:
--   Stabilisers in Γ versus in ±Γ
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be an arbitrary subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and let $\tau$ be a point of the upper half-plane $\mathfrak{H}$, on which $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ acts by Möbius transformations. Form the subgroup $\Gamma \sqcup \langle -1 \rangle$ generated by $\Gamma$ together with the integer powers of $-I$, that is, the join $\Gamma \vee \langle -1\rangle$ inside $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and also the intersection $\Gamma \cap \langle -1\rangle$. Taking each of these subgroups as a group in its own right, acting on $\mathfrak{H}$ by restriction, the assertion is the identity of natural numbers $$\#\mathrm{Stab}_{\Gamma \vee \langle -1\rangle}(\tau) \cdot \#\bigl(\Gamma \cap \langle -1 \rangle\bigr) = 2 \cdot \#\mathrm{Stab}_{\Gamma}(\tau),$$ where all cardinalities are the natural-number cardinalities `Nat.card`, so that an infinite set contributes the value $0$. No finiteness, discreteness or finite-index hypothesis is imposed on $\Gamma$, and no hypothesis relates $\tau$ to $\Gamma$; the second factor on the left is $2$ or $1$ according as $-I$ lies in $\Gamma$ or not.
--
--   This is the standard bookkeeping identity relating the stabiliser of a point of $\mathfrak{H}$ in $\Gamma$ to its stabiliser in $\pm\Gamma = \Gamma\{\pm I\}$, i.e. the passage between $\Gamma$ and its image in $\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, which governs the factor $2$ occurring in the orders of isotropy groups at elliptic points and in the periods of elliptic elements. It is used in the computation of Hecke-type divisors supported at a single point of a modular curve, via [`ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf.heckeDivHBar_single_pt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionaryOf.heckeDivHBar_single_pt).
